\section{Implementation Strategies}\label{sec:effect-impl}

\subsection{Effect Analysis Pass}\label{sec:effect-analysis}

An effect analysis pass computes the effects of each operation, block, and function:

\begin{algorithm}[H]
\caption{Effect Analysis}\label{alg:effect-analysis}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\Function{AnalyzeEffects}{$\mathrm{IR}$}
  \For{each operation $op$}
    \State $\mathrm{effects}(op) \gets \mathrm{intrinsic\_effects}(op)$
    \If{$op$ is a call}
      \State $\mathrm{effects}(op) \gets \mathrm{effects}(op) \cup \mathrm{callee\_effects}(op)$
    \EndIf
  \EndFor
  \For{each block $B$}
    \State $\mathrm{effects}(B) \gets \bigcup_{op \in B} \mathrm{effects}(op)$
  \EndFor
  \For{each function $f$}
    \State $\mathrm{effects}(f) \gets \bigcup_{B \in f} \mathrm{effects}(B)$
  \EndFor
\EndFunction
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\subsection{Effect-Guided Optimization Pipeline}\label{sec:effect-pipeline}

The optimization pipeline uses effect information at each stage:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Early cleanup.} Use effect information for DCE and CSE.
  \item \textbf{Inlining.} Inline pure functions aggressively; be conservative with effectful functions.
  \item \textbf{Loop optimization.} Hoist pure operations; respect effect ordering for effectful operations.
  \item \textbf{Parallelization.} Parallelize pure loops; sequentialize effectful loops.
  \item \textbf{Code generation.} Use effect information for register allocation (pure values can be recomputed instead of spilled).
\end{enumerate}

\begin{historical}
Effect tracking in IRs has evolved from simple ``side-effect-free'' flags (as in LLVM's \texttt{readnone} and \texttt{readonly} attributes) to comprehensive effect systems integrated into the IR. The development of algebraic effects (see \cref{ch:effect-systems}) has provided a theoretical foundation for effect tracking, and modern compilers like Koka and the GHC optimizer have implemented effect-aware IRs that enable aggressive optimization based on effect information.
\end{historical}

