\section{Summary and Further Reading}\label{sec:summary-59}

Effect-aware IRs track side effects as first-class information, enabling the compiler to reason about purity, reorder operations safely, and specialize code based on effect profiles. The key design decisions are the effect lattice (what effects to track), the annotation mechanism (how to attach effects to operations), and the optimization strategies (how to use effect information).

For further reading, we recommend the LLVM language reference on function attributes~\cite{llvm2024}, the Koka language paper~\cite{leijen2019}, and the GHC optimizer documentation.
